269
00:14:16,340 --> 00:14:18,340
We won't let you win!

270
00:14:18,340 --> 00:14:19,340
Lucky, lucky, lucky, lucky!

271
00:14:19,340 --> 00:14:20,340
This battle of wills!

272
00:14:20,340 --> 00:14:21,340
Go, go, go, go!

273
00:14:24,340 --> 00:14:27,340
Both teams are masters of defense and unwilling to back down.

274
00:14:28,340 --> 00:14:31,340
You can feel the tension from the court all over the arena, Chip!

275
00:14:35,340 --> 00:14:37,340
I should've just told them I'd work extra hard the third set

276
00:14:37,340 --> 00:14:39,340
and ask to sit out for the second.

277
00:14:40,340 --> 00:14:42,340
Why does gravity have to be a thing?

278
00:14:42,340 --> 00:14:44,340
Gravity, you're pissing me off!

279
00:14:44,340 --> 00:14:47,340
If it weren't for gravity, the ball wouldn't fall into our court!

280
00:14:47,340 --> 00:14:49,340
The ball only falls because of stupid gravity!

281
00:14:49,340 --> 00:14:50,340
If we run the moon...

282
00:14:50,340 --> 00:14:51,340
Kenma, focus!

283
00:14:53,340 --> 00:14:55,340
Concentration is the one thing Kenma has in spades,

284
00:14:55,340 --> 00:14:57,340
and even he's starting to lose it.

285
00:14:57,340 --> 00:14:59,340
He won't last much longer.

286
00:14:59,340 --> 00:15:02,340
Well, it looks like you better get warmed up again.

287
00:15:02,340 --> 00:15:03,340
Yes, sir.

288
00:15:03,340 --> 00:15:04,340
Yes, sir.

289
00:15:07,340 --> 00:15:08,340
Okay, well what about you?

290
00:15:08,340 --> 00:15:12,340
Don't try to talk to me about guts when you don't even have any!

291
00:15:13,340 --> 00:15:18,340
Ever since Taurus said that to me, I've been asking myself what that word really means.

292
00:15:19,340 --> 00:15:20,340
Guts.

293
00:15:20,340 --> 00:15:22,340
I've always kind of hated that word.

294
00:15:23,340 --> 00:15:26,340
These days I'm pretty sure society's not too fond of it either.

295
00:15:26,340 --> 00:15:32,340
When people say it, it's like they think it's something you can just turn on whenever you feel like it.

296
00:15:33,340 --> 00:15:35,340
But lately, I've been thinking.

297
00:15:36,340 --> 00:15:39,340
Whether you're one of those who loves the word, or one of those who hates it,

298
00:15:39,340 --> 00:15:45,340
the difficulty level involved in turning it on when you need it is much higher than anyone on either side thinks.

299
00:15:45,340 --> 00:15:49,340
I think guts is an ultimate secret move.

300
00:15:49,340 --> 00:15:55,340
It can only be activated at just the right moment by those who have trained up their bodies and souls.

301
00:15:58,340 --> 00:16:01,340
But it's a special move that I can't use.

302
00:16:01,340 --> 00:16:04,340
All of these rallies have been super long.

303
00:16:06,340 --> 00:16:07,340
Front!

304
00:16:07,340 --> 00:16:08,340
One touch!

305
00:16:09,340 --> 00:16:10,340
Get to the ball.

306
00:16:11,340 --> 00:16:12,340
A half step quicker.

307
00:16:12,340 --> 00:16:16,340
That half step will give you what you need to control the ball.

308
00:16:17,340 --> 00:16:19,340
The fatigue has got to be getting to them by now.

309
00:16:20,340 --> 00:16:21,340
They can't last forever.

310
00:16:22,340 --> 00:16:25,340
But their plays are still so measured and deliberate.

311
00:16:28,340 --> 00:16:29,340
They know we're baiting them.

312
00:16:29,340 --> 00:16:31,340
They know we can attack from either side.

313
00:16:32,340 --> 00:16:33,340
They're watching for every possibility.

314
00:16:34,340 --> 00:16:35,340
When that happens, you keep it simple.

315
00:16:36,340 --> 00:16:37,340
And go straight to the middle.

316
00:16:39,340 --> 00:16:40,340
And there's break points!

317
00:16:40,340 --> 00:16:43,340
Nekama is finally able to sit the scales!

318
00:16:44,340 --> 00:16:45,340
Way to go, Kuro!

319
00:16:46,340 --> 00:16:49,340
Because you guys can all use guts.

320
00:16:50,340 --> 00:16:54,340
I bet you're over there thinking you can't do this.

321
00:16:55,340 --> 00:16:56,340
It's true.

322
00:16:56,340 --> 00:16:58,340
You never try and stand your ground.

323
00:16:58,340 --> 00:17:00,340
And you're always looking for ways to get out of stuff.

324
00:17:00,340 --> 00:17:05,340
But even if you were last, or if you were whining the whole time,

325
00:17:06,340 --> 00:17:09,340
whether our coaches and upperclassmen were watching or not,

326
00:17:10,340 --> 00:17:12,340
you always see things through until the end!

327
00:17:12,340 --> 00:17:13,340
Zari!

328
00:17:14,340 --> 00:17:15,340
Cover!

329
00:17:16,340 --> 00:17:18,340
Zari!

330
00:17:18,340 --> 00:17:22,340
Now, Fukunaga's on the left.

331
00:17:22,340 --> 00:17:23,340
He's good, so he'll still be able to make that point, even if there are blockers.

332
00:17:23,340 --> 00:17:27,380
Zori! Cover!

333
00:17:29,120 --> 00:17:32,100
Right now, Fukunaga's on the left.

334
00:17:32,840 --> 00:17:37,260
He's good, so he'll still be able to make that point, even if there are blockers.

335
00:17:38,800 --> 00:17:41,580
So does your school have a good volleyball team, or what?

336
00:17:43,280 --> 00:17:44,800
But I'm not good.

337
00:17:49,860 --> 00:17:51,540
We are together.

338
00:17:53,340 --> 00:18:10,140
I've only ever seen him do that after an A-Pass.

339
00:18:10,580 --> 00:18:14,080
With minimal movement, he performs a perfect set.

340
00:18:14,080 --> 00:18:39,960
And there it is, Joe, after the seemingly endless deuce victory is finally found by Nekamaha.

341
00:18:39,960 --> 00:18:42,660
That was well played by Kozume.

342
00:18:42,900 --> 00:18:47,980
Not once did he ever give the blockers a chance to read him for a second during that entire game.

343
00:18:48,120 --> 00:18:50,360
He truly gave everything he had out there.

344
00:18:50,620 --> 00:18:52,420
Not bad, stolen bread.

345
00:18:52,420 --> 00:19:02,340
Thank you very much for coming!

346
00:19:06,260 --> 00:19:07,440
Thank you for coming!

347
00:19:07,440 --> 00:19:11,860
We'll have to try harder next time.

348
00:19:12,320 --> 00:19:13,620
Your boys really hung tough.

349
00:19:14,320 --> 00:19:15,540
Defense Master Nekamaha.

350
00:19:16,260 --> 00:19:19,240
I thought by this point, you'd be a lot less warlike.

351
00:19:20,200 --> 00:19:25,320
Well, to be perfectly honest, sometimes the boys themselves are more warlike than I am.

352
00:19:25,320 --> 00:19:31,140
That said, I want you to know you're worthy opponents.

353
00:19:31,900 --> 00:19:32,900
Very well played.

354
00:19:36,900 --> 00:19:37,800
Thank you, sir.

355
00:19:37,800 --> 00:19:43,560
You really stood firm today, Kenma.

356
00:19:43,760 --> 00:19:45,060
I barely believe it.

357
00:19:45,480 --> 00:19:49,720
Who would have thought you would suggest a plan that would basically make you pass out if it worked?

358
00:19:50,000 --> 00:19:54,140
I just pushed myself during the second set so we wouldn't have to play a third one.

359
00:19:54,520 --> 00:19:56,500
There's no way I could do three sets of that.

360
00:19:57,020 --> 00:19:59,000
Sarakawa would have crushed me into dust.

361
00:20:00,260 --> 00:20:01,200
So, hey, Kenma.

362
00:20:01,360 --> 00:20:03,960
When you fell earlier, was that all a part of the act, too?

363
00:20:04,260 --> 00:20:06,860
I'm not really a good enough actor to fake that.

364
00:20:07,360 --> 00:20:08,120
Oh, sure.

365
00:20:08,200 --> 00:20:08,820
That makes sense.

366
00:20:09,840 --> 00:20:11,480
You finally showed some guts, Kenma.

367
00:20:11,900 --> 00:20:12,980
I really didn't.

368
00:20:13,680 --> 00:20:15,800
I'm not a high enough level to use guts.

369
00:20:16,360 --> 00:20:16,660
What?

370
00:20:17,480 --> 00:20:19,840
I guess it was just that, oh, I don't know.

371
00:20:20,180 --> 00:20:22,020
I felt like I owed you guys.

372
00:20:22,300 --> 00:20:27,340
You were all working so hard to get the ball up for me that I felt I had to do my part, too.

373
00:20:27,800 --> 00:20:28,300
I guess.

374
00:20:28,820 --> 00:20:30,020
That's what I'm saying.

375
00:20:30,300 --> 00:20:31,160
That was guts.

376
00:20:31,200 --> 00:20:32,940
Look, I just did what I could, okay?

377
00:20:33,080 --> 00:20:34,900
Do you really have to put a label on everything?

378
00:20:34,900 --> 00:20:36,620
Is it that weird for me to work for something?

379
00:20:36,620 --> 00:20:37,400
What are you so mad about?

380
00:20:37,820 --> 00:20:41,260
Speaking of, I think I heard you getting mad at gravity during that set.

381
00:20:41,640 --> 00:20:42,420
Okay, man.

382
00:20:42,580 --> 00:20:45,040
Your personality changes way too much when you're tired.

383
00:20:45,280 --> 00:20:46,520
You must be low on carbohydrates.

384
00:20:47,200 --> 00:20:48,540
You should probably have a banana.

385
00:20:50,880 --> 00:20:53,780
Is it so weird for someone to put in some effort for their team?

386
00:20:54,080 --> 00:20:54,320
Huh?

387
00:20:54,700 --> 00:20:56,260
Or is it just weird when I do it?

388
00:20:56,320 --> 00:20:56,800
That it?

389
00:20:57,300 --> 00:20:57,980
Oh, man.

390
00:20:57,980 --> 00:21:00,740
You, you try!

391
00:21:01,440 --> 00:21:01,960
Oh, God!

392
00:21:02,360 --> 00:21:03,260
You stay away!

393
00:21:03,880 --> 00:21:05,440
Yamamoto's overreacting again.

394
00:21:05,940 --> 00:21:06,660
Not this time.

395
00:21:06,680 --> 00:21:07,440
You finally showed us your guts!

396
00:21:07,440 --> 00:21:11,320
It's pretty rare for Kenma to admit he's part of a group, so I'd say that reaction is fair.

397
00:21:14,280 --> 00:21:15,380
Give me a hug!

398
00:21:15,460 --> 00:21:16,040
Back, animals!

399
00:21:16,600 --> 00:21:18,360
Fukunaga, please don't encourage him!

400
00:21:18,500 --> 00:21:18,560
No, man, you do!

401
00:21:18,560 --> 00:21:25,320
Now, if only Kenma could be half as aggressive whenever he's playing volleyball, as he gets

402
00:21:25,320 --> 00:21:28,100
when he's in his own world playing his stupid video games...

403
00:21:28,100 --> 00:21:30,180
Don't narrate your own version of my thoughts.

404
00:21:31,120 --> 00:21:33,440
On second thought, I still hate guts.

405
00:21:33,820 --> 00:21:35,900
The difficulty level is just too high.

406
00:21:38,900 --> 00:21:42,100
But, I definitely leveled up.

407
00:21:42,540 --> 00:21:46,140
And if we're gonna play, I wanna fight the strongest bosses.

408
00:21:48,560 --> 00:21:58,540
I guess there's one guy that gets Kenma to start acting aggressive, so that's good.

409
00:21:58,700 --> 00:21:59,520
Heck yeah!

410
00:22:00,720 --> 00:22:03,160
So, Karasuno's up against the Mia twins.

411
00:22:03,280 --> 00:22:05,960
Whoa, it looks like they already took the first set off those guys.

412
00:22:07,000 --> 00:22:07,400
Hmm.

413
00:22:08,240 --> 00:22:09,580
Guess what, Karasuno?

414
00:22:11,340 --> 00:22:12,180
We're here.

415
00:22:18,560 --> 00:22:21,800
And now, we're coming for you.

416
00:22:21,800 --> 00:22:22,800
And now, we're coming for you.

417
00:22:23,240 --> 00:22:26,200
確かなことはいつか

418
00:22:26,200 --> 00:22:29,000
わかるときが来るから

419
00:22:29,000 --> 00:22:31,500
街が立っていさ

420
00:22:31,500 --> 00:22:35,800
今、思いを止めないで

421
00:22:35,800 --> 00:22:48,640
街が立っていさ

422
00:22:48,640 --> 00:22:49,980
現実が飛んじゃうような

423
00:22:49,980 --> 00:22:52,900
夢が欲しかったのに

424
00:22:52,900 --> 00:22:57,520
辻褄を合わすだけの日々は

425
00:22:57,520 --> 00:22:59,140
味気ない

426
00:22:59,140 --> 00:23:02,300
何にも怖くなんて泣いて

427
00:23:02,300 --> 00:23:05,440
強がって馬鹿の少年が

428
00:23:05,440 --> 00:23:09,240
今もまだ汗ばむ背中を

429
00:23:09,240 --> 00:23:11,280
見つめてるから

430
00:23:11,280 --> 00:23:14,500
奇跡はもういらない

431
00:23:14,500 --> 00:23:17,960
どこまでだって

432
00:23:17,960 --> 00:23:19,860
いける僕らは

433
00:23:19,860 --> 00:23:20,820
ファンデ

434
00:23:20,820 --> 00:23:22,820
夢も叶うさ

435
00:23:22,820 --> 00:23:25,760
ここまでやってきたのは

436
00:23:25,760 --> 00:23:28,760
偶然なんかじゃなくて

437
00:23:28,760 --> 00:23:31,800
去ってしまう舞台に

438
00:23:31,800 --> 00:23:32,800
だって

439
00:23:32,800 --> 00:23:33,800
痛いと

440
00:23:33,800 --> 00:23:34,600
いつでも

441
00:23:34,600 --> 00:23:37,640
強く願い続けた

442
00:23:37,640 --> 00:23:38,640
君が

443
00:23:38,640 --> 00:23:40,760
そこにいたから

444
00:23:40,760 --> 00:23:54,840
次回は

445
00:23:54,840 --> 00:23:56,320
The Ultimate Challengers

446
00:23:56,320 --> 00:23:58,460
ファンデ

